atlas external

architecture remote-mesh-transport
  canonical_name RemoteMeshTransport
  family external
  domain External / Federation
  layer external/transport
  semantic_question Did this coordination envelope arrive as the bytes its producer addressed, and what happens when it did not?
  purpose Content-addressed sanitized envelopes on a public non-merge branch between local Run8 carriers and external operator trajectories. The address is taken over the whole envelope minus the address field, so any post-seal edit unbinds it. A refused envelope is quarantined with BOTH the declared and the measured address rather than dropped, because an address disagreement is two carriers disagreeing about content, not malformed input. Export converges on content: identical bytes already at an address have already succeeded; different bytes there are a collision that is never resolved by overwriting.
  maturity implemented
  # Demoted: every witness this carried was archived. The evidence was
  # retired and the claim was never revisited, which is the laundering the
  # atlas forbids -- reclaiming measured needs a witness that runs today.
  known_gap remote-mesh-transport lost its live witness to archival and holds implemented until one runs again
  node_types MeshEnvelope
  node_types QuarantinedEnvelope
  node_types ExportState
  node_types CoordinationObligation
  node_types DeliveryReceipt
  edge_types addresses
  edge_types quarantines
  edge_types diverges_from
  edge_types materializes_as_work
  state_types admitted
  state_types duplicate
  state_types quarantined
  state_types synced
  state_types collision
  state_types refused
  state_types delivered
  state_types acknowledged
  state_types acknowledgement_refused
  invariant the declared address must equal the address measured over the envelope's own content
  invariant an already-seen event id never bypasses validation of the bytes currently present on the remote branch
  invariant one event id cannot be rebound to different content; both addresses are retained as a collision
  invariant a refused envelope is retained with both addresses, never silently dropped
  invariant re-presenting a quarantined envelope increments an attempt count instead of re-refusing it invisibly
  invariant the privacy gate runs on import as well as export, so an upstream leak never becomes our publication
  invariant structured raw prompt, stdout, stderr, raw log, private correspondence, and authority-grant fields are refused
  invariant a divergence report carries the two addresses and never echoes the refused content
  invariant an actionable provider-authored event addressed to another local carrier materializes as idempotent WorkGraph state that excludes its author
  invariant the WorkGraph id of a mesh obligation is injective in the event id, so two distinct legal envelopes can never collapse onto one obligation and silently drop the second
  invariant a receipt can acknowledge only an existing delivery to the same provider; it cannot manufacture delivery
  invariant the originating provider cannot acknowledge a cross-provider obligation that excludes it
  invariant the privacy gate reads every string in the envelope, list positions included, so evidence_refs, audience, changed_paths and tests[].command are inspected rather than skipped
  invariant the set of acknowledgements the eligibility fence would refuse today is empty; a closure written before the fence existed is reopened, with the prior closure preserved verbatim
  invariant repeated valid acknowledgement preserves the first consumption receipt rather than replacing it
  invariant durable store guards enforce delivery and cross-provider acknowledgement eligibility even when a long-running carrier still has pre-upgrade Python loaded
  invariant pre-fence ineligible acknowledgements are retracted from the live frontier while their original ReceiptEnvelope assertion remains auditable
  invariant a successful write is not synchronized until remote readback bytes exactly equal the local payload
  invariant concurrent first export attempts converge through atomic bookkeeping rather than a unique-key failure
  invariant a terminal exact-readback receipt recovers a crash before EventGraph export-state projection without another remote write
  invariant concurrent importers serialize the shared tracking-ref update and inspect one immutable commit snapshot per cycle
  invariant a partial import or export failure is explicitly degraded even though bounded maintenance remains nonfatal
  forbidden_inference a delivered mesh message -> an authority grant
  forbidden_inference a delivered mesh message -> a completion receipt
  forbidden_inference an admitted envelope -> its claims are true
  forbidden_inference a projection that inserted no row -> the obligation was already held
  forbidden_inference an address collision -> permission to force-push the transport branch
  forbidden_inference the transport branch -> a merge target
  computational_form durable
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/mesh_transport.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_mesh_transport.py.archive
  known_gap the producer side of the mesh is external, so a re-sealed envelope cannot be proven to arrive; only its refusal can be reported back
  known_gap divergence_report and mark_divergence_reported have no production caller; the remote-mesh-quarantines-into-divergence interaction is exercised only by its unit witness, so on 2026-08-21 sixteen quarantined envelopes carried 8385 cumulative refused re-fetch attempts with divergence_reported still 0 for every row and no producer notified
  known_gap quarantined and divergence_report call ensure_schema, so an observer holding a read-only handle to live coordination state cannot read the divergence backlog through the module's own API
  known_gap envelopes published before the list-traversal fix are already public; the gate can refuse republication but cannot unpublish local-2b5745a7e20f61978cfcdbb81409, whose body carried a home path
  source_lineage Run8 federated mesh; live 2026-08-21 refusal of two external envelopes whose declared address did not bind their bytes
  source_lineage 2026-08-21 cross-provider replay of proof challenge local-746b1d0bc6cbc4467780842d8046: the routing fence held on all 14 checks, and the adversarial pass found the privacy gate never descended into lists
  source_lineage 2026-08-21 second cross-provider replay of the same challenge under changed state (118 events, 136 work items, mesh branch eeb84c24): the fence held again, and the adversarial pass found the work-id stem was not injective -- ':' is legal in an event id but folds to '-', and ids may reach 180 characters against a 120-character stem, so a second distinct obligation was dropped and reported as an ordinary idempotent replay

architecture mesh-routing-replay
  owns MeshRoutingReplay
  consumes MeshEvent
  consumes WorkState
  publishes ReplayVerdict
  canonical_name MeshRoutingReplay
  family external
  domain External / Federation
  layer external/proof
  semantic_question Does this envelope's claimed cross-provider routing actually hold in live state, and does replaying it change anything?
  purpose Replays one published mesh envelope against live EventGraph, WorkGraph, delivery and public-branch state, re-deriving the route from the envelope instead of trusting the stored row, and mutating a snapshot so a proof run cannot damage the frontier it measures.
  maturity measured
  node_types ReplayCheck
  node_types RoutingCase
  edge_types replays
  edge_types refutes
  state_types review_result
  state_types trace_divergence
  internal_calculus address rebinding over reconstructed EventGraph state
  internal_calculus route re-derivation and adversarial author/audience mutation matrix
  invariant the route is recomputed from the envelope; agreement with the stored row is a check, never an assumption
  invariant replay runs against a SQLite backup copy, so a proof never mutates the coordination frontier it measures
  invariant a replayed projection that creates a row, or a re-admission that is not a duplicate, is a failed proof rather than a repair
  invariant the mutation matrix must show the fence reacting to the author and audience, because a constant answer proves nothing
  invariant the replay probes obligation-id injectivity in both lossy directions, because a dropped obligation and an honest idempotent replay are otherwise indistinguishable
  invariant every mesh work id in live state must re-derive from a live event id, so an injectivity repair cannot orphan an obligation the frontier already owns
  invariant the emitted artifact is repo-relative and quotable onto the public branch
  forbidden_inference a passing replay -> the envelope's claims are true
  forbidden_inference a passing replay -> authority to perform the challenge's requested effects
  forbidden_inference a snapshot replay -> the live frontier was exercised under concurrency
  computational_form durable
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/mesh_routing_replay.py.archive
  witness evidence/proofs/mesh-routing-fence-replay.json
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_mesh_transport.py.archive
  known_gap replay measures a snapshot, so it cannot observe a race between two carriers writing the same delivery row
  known_gap only the local side is replayed; an external producer's own state remains unobservable
  source_lineage Run8 cross-provider proof challenge local-746b1d0bc6cbc4467780842d8046, authored by codex and assigned away from codex; executed 2026-08-21 with 14/14 checks passing against mesh branch commit fb814c3c
  source_lineage re-executed 2026-08-21 against mesh branch commit eeb84c24 with 17/17 checks, three of them added by that run after it refuted the obligation-id derivation
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
